Source: rmac
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jacob Samas <samasjacob@icloud.com>
Rules-Requires-Root: no
# The same libraries and tools release.yml's build-amd64 job installs. There
# is deliberately no rustc or cargo here: like the niri packages, the build
# uses the rustup toolchain pinned in rust-toolchain.toml (1.95.0), which the
# Ubuntu archive does not carry. dpkg-checkbuilddeps cannot see it, so
# scripts/linux/build-rmac-source-package.sh checks for cargo itself.
Build-Depends: clang,
               dpkg-dev,
               libfontconfig1-dev,
               libfreetype-dev,
               libssl-dev,
               libvulkan-dev,
               libwayland-dev,
               libx11-xcb-dev,
               libxcb-render0-dev,
               libxcb-shape0-dev,
               libxcb-xfixes0-dev,
               libxcb1-dev,
               libxkbcommon-dev,
               libxkbcommon-x11-dev,
               pkg-config,
               python3,
               xz-utils
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/millionrust/lulo

Package: rmac-apps
Section: utils
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Description: macOS-inspired applications for the rmac Linux desktop
 Provides Files, Terminal, Notes, Text Editor, System Monitor, Calculator,
 Preview, Archive Utility, Clock, Apps, and Settings with their original rmac
 desktop metadata and assets.

Package: rmac-session
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Description: niri-based rmac Wayland desktop session
 Provides the supervised rmac shell services, GDM session entry, portal
 selection, secure-lock integration, and immutable session defaults while
 retaining stock GNOME as the recovery session.
